      why: 'Carbon weighs 12, oxygen 16: 16 kg of methane grabs 64 kg of oxygen to make 44 kg of CO₂ and 36 kg of water. The chimney mass is mostly imported from the air — which is why fuel-to-emissions arithmetic is stoichiometry you can do in your head.',
